  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 2D Offset pass that starts Inside or Outside round a part now enters by the Arc entry from the air outside the stock box (new module `crates/motion/src/machining2d/air_entry.rs`).\n\n1. The tool plunges in air at a point P. The distance from P to the stock box is at least the tool radius plus `approach_distance` (#3745).\n2. In the cut plane, a straight lead in air (tangent to the arc), then one G17 arc of Arc radius and Arc sweep, tangent to the first cut at the pass start. A change of Arc radius or Arc sweep changes the arc in the output.\n3. The lead is proved with the proof of the horizontal arc entry (`descent_xy::arc_at`, made `pub(super)`) against the cutter-centre area joined with the air outside the box, and across none of the planned passes. Thus it touches no part and crosses no ring.\n4. When no air lead fits, the entry stands down to a named helix, then a named ramp along the first cut, else the op is refused by name (`AIR_ENTRY_REFUSAL`, read by `approach::refusal`). The axial dive and the vertical arc ramp into material are no longer stand-ins.\n5. A re-entry after a lift onto a start in material (`entry_restart`) tries the air entry first. On a start-side pass it then tries a clear helix before the named plunge.\n6. The avoid route (fixtures and clamps, #3810): each level takes the same air room, less that level's keep-outs over the whole descent. A plunge or lead that would touch a fixture or a clamp is not proved, so the entry moves or stands down by name.\n\nInside: the other rings enclose the first Inside ring, so each lead from the air crosses rings at the cut Z. The verifier's Crossing law holds such a post. Thus Inside takes the named helix (or ramp), never a plunge into material. The decision and the dropped options are in `docs/decisions/3746-air-entry.md`.\n\nThe pass links (`level_link`, `pass_link`, `link_proof`) are not changed (#3747 owns them).\n\n## Readings (dog bone, 80 x 50 stock box, D8, stepover 2, Arc entry)\n\n- Before: Outside plunged at (39.400, -24.400), 0.000 mm off the stock box, note \"the arc's lead room is blocked - axial dive on the floor instead\". Inside entered with the vertical arc, whose first chords are a plunge into material by `plunge_law::first_solid_plunge`.\n- After: Outside plunges 6 mm or more off the box (R 4 + approach 2); the first cut is a G17 arc of radius 8 (Arc radius 0) and a quarter turn (Arc sweep 0); radius 6 / 10 and sweep 60 show in the output. Inside: no plunge into material; the entry is named.\n- fig8 Outside, Arc entry: each level is entered from the air with a first arc. After the merge of #3818, four pass links still lift across the part to a start inside ring 0, and those re-entries plunge into material, named. An air lead would cross ring 0 at the cut Z; no helix or ramp fits clear of the cut rings. The cause is the link code: #3825.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` lib, `machining2d::air_entry::tests`: `outside_entry_plunges_in_air`, `outside_first_cut_is_an_arc_in_the_plane`, `arc_radius_changes_the_lead`, `inside_entry_is_no_plunge_into_material`, `outside_entry_is_no_plunge_into_material`. All five were red with the air room off (the `main` behaviour) and are green now.\n- `camcraft-app` `offset_pass_start` (heavy): `fig8_start_sides_enter_from_the_air` (green).\n- `camcraft-motion` lib: `avoid_route_entry_plunges_in_air_clear_of_a_clamp` (#3810; red with the avoid air room off).\n- `fig8_outside_offset_has_no_plunge_into_material`: known-fail #3825 (still red after #3818: the four re-entry plunges come from pass-link lifts).\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the head after the merge of origin/main (with #3818):\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6): 172 steps, 0 failed.\n- Targeted heavy step `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: offset_pass_start\"`: ok; the gate skipped the known-fail pin of #3825.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test offset_pass_start -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A user-selected Helix, Ramp or Plunge keeps its entry; its warning and the Arc default are #3748.\n- The Lead in / Lead out page already offers all four kinds for each start side and greys none out (`lead_page.rs`). No UI change.\n- The light lane was not run.\n- `descent.rs` was 411 lines and is 418 now (the new `Descent::Air` arms).\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset \"Pass starts at\" Inside and Outside: the Arc entry plunges in air outside the stock box (tool radius plus the approach distance) and arcs onto the first ring in the cut plane with the Arc radius and Arc sweep; where no air entry fits, a named helix or ramp is used, never a plunge into material.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #3746\nFixes #3810\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
